#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119743 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119559 :question/id #uuid "98c98a56-ca57-5dc6-9dc4-c40da53806f7" :question/math-academy-id "e-3063" :question/problem "Write down the integral that gives the arc length of the curve  $\\mathbf f (t) = \\langle 3 \\sin t, \\: 2\\sin 2t \\rangle$\nfrom $t =\\dfrac {3\\pi} 2$  to $t = 2\\pi.$\n\n![](images/57/574a16e843a9c81e5fc9ddbbe2c0dc2c308ffcac4991bcbf48c7f45b4871c93b.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf f'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf f'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡2t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4fc0992a-423e-5023-98d5-9d53c3b77788" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048999 :topic/math-academy-id 4139 :topic/title "Differentiating Vector-Valued Functions"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050860 :topic/math-academy-id 997 :topic/title "The Arc Length of a Parametric Curve"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051021 :topic/math-academy-id 1277 :topic/title "Calculating the Magnitude of Cartesian Vectors in 3D"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120272 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c60eb52-e275-5f9e-8b64-8f24c6fbbbff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{2\\cos^{2} 2t + 3\\sin^{2} 3t}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117772} {:answer/id #uuid "5068c443-8395-505c-92d8-71cea0dfc17e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{4\\cos^{2} 2t + 9\\sin^{2} 3t}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117773} {:answer/id #uuid "748e7d72-d682-5524-af39-e923fed4a5ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{4\\sin^{2} 2t + 9\\cos^{2} 3t}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117774} {:answer/id #uuid "7997a0c6-f7e9-5d98-aedd-32f939d3e168" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{2\\sin^{2} 2t + 9\\cos^{2} 3t}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117775} {:answer/id #uuid "7eb306df-b1bd-5be5-b18b-0285d0ccf69e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{π}\\sqrt{2\\cos^{2} 2t + 9\\sin^{2} 3t}dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117776}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6e0ba63d-f616-5753-b3ec-5ef064c6cb5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117771} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc3dbeb4-85f0-5977-97bc-032932c84bc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡2t+9{sin}^{2}⁡3t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391649} {:answer/id #uuid "769deadf-6f4e-5979-ab29-41e31ac33156" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡2t+9{cos}^{2}⁡3t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391650} {:answer/id #uuid "8acb4dd0-ab7b-50a4-bed8-752a2b64b388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡2t+9{sin}^{2}⁡3t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391651} {:answer/id #uuid "4b968ecc-eb2e-5899-bdd8-779a4c1f182d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡2t+3{sin}^{2}⁡3t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391652} {:answer/id #uuid "0ec6159d-f7de-5b2f-b124-7ba4b0ab6ebc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{2{sin}^{2}⁡2t+9{cos}^{2}⁡3t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8acb4dd0-ab7b-50a4-bed8-752a2b64b388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡2t+9{sin}^{2}⁡3t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391651} :answer-field/id #uuid "438187f3-2ea9-5adc-8e76-df9ae09801fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391648}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "994d254c-8dfb-50db-8abf-3c167a677836" :question/math-academy-id "q-33728" :question/problem "![](images/d1/d162245ac19c3ef9ae63d602fb4e188ddfd241a1a604304f6c272c3902ce1e93.png)\n\nWhich integral expression gives the arc length of the curve $g(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t⟩$ from $t=0$ to $t=\\pi ?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${g}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{g}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}+(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡2t+9{sin}^{2}⁡3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡2t+9{sin}^{2}⁡3t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120281 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7002bf97-f2f4-584e-9358-9901bcdc36c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+5}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312858} {:answer/id #uuid "c02b3e07-f8b1-5a36-8107-54957d2ec5d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313481} {:answer/id #uuid "db80e8bf-9842-5c6d-bd83-4583ec9425fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+4}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313702} {:answer/id #uuid "e797d87f-61ea-5692-b189-9f791eb47e1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+6}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313811} {:answer/id #uuid "f08c0c47-5ca9-5225-ad0d-e2d99574aadd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{t}(t+2)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e797d87f-61ea-5692-b189-9f791eb47e1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+6}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313811} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc1df9aa-037a-519b-b947-a899bc624f42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314526}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3bc45ddc-02bd-5a1e-bfa3-f99f90a0c552" :question/math-academy-id "q-33862" :question/problem "Which integral  expression gives the arc length of the curve $f(t)={e}^{t}(\\,i+2\\,j+t\\,k)$ from  $t=1$ to $t=2?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{f}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{e}^{t})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t{e}^{t})\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\,i+2{e}^{t}\\,j+(t{e}^{t}+{e}^{t})\\,k \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{({e}^{t})^{2}+(2{e}^{t})^{2}+({e}^{t}(t+1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+4{e}^{2t}+{e}^{2t}({t}^{2}+2t+1)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}(1+4+{t}^{2}+2t+1)} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{e}^{t}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+6}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262772 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "786fd2f0-0c3d-5b7a-b5bc-a3608fc69fb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{16{cos}^{2}⁡t+9}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260929} {:answer/id #uuid "91d23bb2-32fb-5fbc-9842-9fb48c39267d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{3{cos}^{2}⁡t+4}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261143} {:answer/id #uuid "9501dc4d-d6ab-5f38-966b-90a4a703d054" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{9{sin}^{2}⁡t+16}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261170} {:answer/id #uuid "dac1fd6a-eb18-58b7-911b-730ac1c804e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{4{sin}^{2}⁡t+3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261807} {:answer/id #uuid "fe36bad1-4fa4-557e-a374-9f534fc494fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe36bad1-4fa4-557e-a374-9f534fc494fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262105} :answer-field/id #uuid "f53642b3-fa2e-5032-9340-8b9099d29395" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262549}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d1a4d542-8890-5129-a744-baf652c9fc9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-127419" :question/problem "Which integral expression gives the arc length of the curve $f(t)=⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ from $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{f}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡t+9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)+9{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{9{cos}^{2}⁡t+16}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262773 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "214ab720-6ecf-5a54-bbca-66e11f886130" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260158} {:answer/id #uuid "491c9a30-b37c-5794-9dfe-c72bf6a272ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{2{e}^{t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260507} {:answer/id #uuid "741301d8-03d2-596d-99cb-dea017a15918" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{t}+2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260889} {:answer/id #uuid "99f9d829-a8f9-5d96-a7b8-f240b15576e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{2{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261210} {:answer/id #uuid "9a64fc13-46c7-54cc-b859-06bfde01dc08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "214ab720-6ecf-5a54-bbca-66e11f886130" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260158} :answer-field/id #uuid "83cdb749-1449-536c-beab-38d88342a23d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262347}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ae63a631-2f65-575f-9860-3fcf3ba50584" :question/math-academy-id "q-127427" :question/problem "Which integral expression gives the arc length of the curve $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩$ from $t=-1$ to $t=1?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{f}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+({e}^{t})^{2}+{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+{e}^{2t}+{cos}^{2}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+2({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+2}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314703 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2208ccc5-5934-51e2-b52d-8ff31bed4e36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312232} {:answer/id #uuid "65d3df9b-2970-5299-ab99-547382b11901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312777} {:answer/id #uuid "7ce9c1bd-fb44-5c82-b8e8-5b81f7969c0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312977} {:answer/id #uuid "a95d6aed-c1ec-5c63-b9a8-8a0ba8e816ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313302} {:answer/id #uuid "b5c14440-88e2-525d-85e7-2db79078355d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡2t-{sin}^{2}⁡2t+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a95d6aed-c1ec-5c63-b9a8-8a0ba8e816ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313302} :answer-field/id #uuid "9762ce0e-0f2a-5c5c-ad7d-6b8b6bc424c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314419}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "732ad1b9-5772-5700-8754-f590c45d555d" :question/math-academy-id "q-33857" :question/problem "Which integral  expression gives the arc length of the curve $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,{t}^{2}⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=1?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{f}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{f}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}+(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)^{2}+(2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡2t+4{sin}^{2}⁡2t+4{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({cos}^{2}⁡2t+{sin}^{2}⁡2t+{t}^{2})} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}‖{f}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{1}2\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391631 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e513d59-ec4b-56e0-a149-748a6164fa0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391633} {:answer/id #uuid "5b08fcdf-1c61-56cb-b330-8a9759c8a89e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391634} {:answer/id #uuid "8210e913-8fc4-50f7-87cd-8fd56787dfec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391635} {:answer/id #uuid "d3b489bc-4e90-59af-8076-7c8a1e2ef20d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+2{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391636} {:answer/id #uuid "d1c3feb9-80f0-5263-bb9b-e4994b84169c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{2+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e513d59-ec4b-56e0-a149-748a6164fa0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391633} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ffd0d69-a63d-58b1-a22c-7c7b302f6577" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391632}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "214d5c25-f05c-5b96-87cf-f66e123da8aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-33706" :question/problem "![](images/10/10ee30ddf508bf985e1c3a41491818723b57301412a5514e4a39c3bc13518acd.png)\n\nWhich integral  expression gives the arc length of the curve $g(t)=⟨t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,2-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=\\pi ?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${g}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{g}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t+{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡t-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392884 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "917fe269-7275-5dbe-8043-5ab73f39f23b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{2{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392886} {:answer/id #uuid "c302b461-16a8-5a13-a604-48e2a5a05708" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{3-{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392887} {:answer/id #uuid "610e92dd-f0e2-5bea-8bb6-5a4d0d844cb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{2+{sin}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392888} {:answer/id #uuid "6f4b7c1f-6178-5bb3-8bfd-e481d21ad116" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{2+{cos}^{2}⁡t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392889} {:answer/id #uuid "c13bb008-eeba-55b4-aec7-73942951b937" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c13bb008-eeba-55b4-aec7-73942951b937" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392890} :answer-field/id #uuid "e342550d-8ba6-5a84-9cad-9202991768dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392885}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "719d5fba-71fa-5184-acdb-743568f97311" :question/math-academy-id "q-64723" :question/problem "![](images/d4/d42e9c6ed71f06c2dec273a91d3a4cfbdf5c58095be9370285d7987d38f7b5a6.png)\n\nWhich integral  expression gives the arc length of the curve $h(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+t\\,k$ from  $t=0$ to $t=2\\pi ?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${h}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{h}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+1\\,k \\\\ ‖{h}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }‖{h}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392891 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b393a27d-b443-5b97-b762-ed6603aad1e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{16{t}^{6}+9{t}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392893} {:answer/id #uuid "66fa210a-e578-5c4d-8132-eb89718f32cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{{t}^{6}+{t}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392894} {:answer/id #uuid "85f0edfc-dff0-5ee7-a4b2-955898d40c67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{8{t}^{5}+9{t}^{3}+6}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392895} {:answer/id #uuid "d8531aa7-d3a8-5834-8493-ee803adaa77f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{5}\\sqrt{16{t}^{6}+9}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392896} {:answer/id #uuid "d88974de-cee3-50ec-af8b-a8554a2c05b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{16{t}^{6}+9{t}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b393a27d-b443-5b97-b762-ed6603aad1e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{16{t}^{6}+9{t}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392893} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e4f8290-db9f-5614-851c-76e4decb0150" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392892}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "93e74816-9928-5c75-b857-debb8b7d37d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-64724" :question/problem "Which integral expression gives the arc length of the curve $r(t)={t}^{3}\\,i+3t\\,j+{t}^{4}\\,k$ from  $t=2$ to $t=5?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4})\\,k \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,i+3\\,j+4{t}^{3}\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(3{t}^{2})^{2}+(3)^{2}+(4{t}^{3})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+9+16{t}^{6}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{2}^{5}\\sqrt{16{t}^{6}+9{t}^{4}+9}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Integral Expression For the Arc Length of a Curve"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119744 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119560 :question/id #uuid "8932c22b-465f-5a48-962c-e53730e5ba40" :question/math-academy-id "e-3064" :question/problem "Find the arc length of the curve $\\mathbf g (t) = \\langle 3 - 2 \\sin 2t, \\: 1 - 2\\cos 2t \\rangle$ from $t=\\dfrac \\pi 3$ to $\\pi.$\n\n![](images/29/29c97e5963d451cc389944ef113764b2d15998448e773a02bb98c062207c2860.png)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf g'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf g'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)^{2}+(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{cos}^{2}⁡2t+16{sin}^{2}⁡2t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4t\\,{|}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =4(\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e310cbe-9d6b-5bc4-960a-8813333bc8be" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049488 :topic/math-academy-id 207 :topic/title "Simplifying Expressions Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120527 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75e5fa3c-091c-520e-8479-d218155399c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343254} {:answer/id #uuid "8b51d751-2961-50bb-98bc-c99dea65a8e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343452} {:answer/id #uuid "8baa903e-69cf-5fab-bf1d-52f2ba066f34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343455} {:answer/id #uuid "c0402a4e-bae1-581e-b109-bffe3d5de024" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343924} {:answer/id #uuid "deebeadd-1734-5b4a-bc84-8d64bed65493" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8baa903e-69cf-5fab-bf1d-52f2ba066f34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343455} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0be3d9a-49eb-5fc8-91bf-4c96b81633a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344886}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d67d847a-8cc9-599e-9782-16c3ef20921d" :question/math-academy-id "q-77065" :question/problem "![](images/b6/b614e2c3e6abf0d7ddb8399aa7ea78b7a0e618a965ee7b5481edf08310a45031.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $g(t)=⟨{t}^{3}-3t,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩$ from $t=1$ to $t=2?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${g}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{g}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-3t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2}-3,\\,6t⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(3{t}^{2}-3)^{2}+(6t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}-18{t}^{2}+9+36{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+18{t}^{2}+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3{t}^{2}+3)^{2}} \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(3{t}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =({t}^{3}+3t){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(8+6)-(1+3) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120528 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42dd07b3-4065-530a-88aa-6e7a0aca511d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342795} {:answer/id #uuid "78d7838b-fe95-5cad-a4c4-269d7bdb904b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343282} {:answer/id #uuid "881ebcca-4863-55f5-9890-dcd0a9df648a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343415} {:answer/id #uuid "8eab15db-b045-510e-8571-aaaaa67b97ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343486} {:answer/id #uuid "fee32fe0-e17a-5ba1-bc6c-a8f5d62a18d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8eab15db-b045-510e-8571-aaaaa67b97ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343486} :answer-field/id #uuid "82eb78e8-3d58-5365-9450-5b95abad2149" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344723}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c0bd5879-0033-526b-bc0b-c6b5d407bf6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-77066" :question/problem "![](images/9b/9b83db0bb11b8e4bbcc4b04b7bf696879d4d7f4732d6aef7d005f9da2b625526.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $g(t)=⟨2{t}^{3/2},\\,3t⟩$ from $t=0$ to $t=3.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${g}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{g}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3/2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\sqrt{t},\\,3⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(3\\sqrt{t})^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9t+9} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{t+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}3\\sqrt{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}3(t+1)^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2(t+1)^{3/2}{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =16-2 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262794 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "094b9b5d-90a5-52e6-ad22-1226b75da63c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{e}^{\\pi }-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259958} {:answer/id #uuid "4077f389-0099-57f1-8340-852121cc2cb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({e}^{\\pi }-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260439} {:answer/id #uuid "6c320932-603e-58a3-a9fc-86f6548e4a8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260824} {:answer/id #uuid "87a3a0e9-f0fa-50c2-9617-655e6d9e094e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{\\pi /2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261056} {:answer/id #uuid "f7a2e11f-134c-5105-9358-e819e1684bb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{e}^{\\pi /2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c320932-603e-58a3-a9fc-86f6548e4a8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260824} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8e0ad00-4b7d-5048-9a17-3b79e4ef2994" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262500}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "76702025-335e-5381-8404-f40fe3fd7dfd" :question/math-academy-id "q-127573" :question/problem "![](images/16/162c0d0310cbbb533c30af373820751fc6c5a447127958486571224d7f8ac07a.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ from $t=0$ to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & ={e}^{t}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =|{e}^{t}|\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\sqrt{2({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{2}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}{e}^{t}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}({e}^{\\pi /2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262798 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "645b7b78-a1b2-5fca-b90e-39d47899cd92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260741} {:answer/id #uuid "88e591c2-1771-5bd4-9969-13cd8f27d0ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261066} {:answer/id #uuid "b7f29c98-2b8a-5e10-afa8-61e4c808e5dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261488} {:answer/id #uuid "c6d54c34-a83c-514e-812b-09d754b2eef3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261632} {:answer/id #uuid "ccd06f32-fb58-584a-a752-9e7577253c10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6d54c34-a83c-514e-812b-09d754b2eef3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261632} :answer-field/id #uuid "df607fbe-708b-5c81-8093-49116a0267c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262513}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1f15b24c-9b34-54f4-8404-a1b55cbcfc8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-127585" :question/problem "![](images/c4/c4aa91668440687bbae4b1f85672f5cbaf7ce00d978049c7558eed99b7361d1a.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨3t-{t}^{3},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩$ from $t=-1$ to $t=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-{t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3-3{t}^{2},\\,6t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(3-3{t}^{2})}^{2}+{(6t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9-18{t}^{2}+9{t}^{4}+36{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+18{t}^{2}+9} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{({t}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =3({t}^{2}+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}3({t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{-1}^{1}({t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+t){|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =3(\\frac{{1}^{3}}{3}+1-[\\frac{(-1)^{3}}{3}+(-1)]) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{3}+1+\\frac{1}{3}+1) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262801 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33362404-a630-58e0-ab60-b015a97a07bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260338} {:answer/id #uuid "8b9f6888-780f-56da-9b96-be6ea61dfe14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261094} {:answer/id #uuid "b0b610b3-0649-5a84-aede-f6eaefb07746" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261437} {:answer/id #uuid "d2902a59-e5b1-5475-92d3-40644cd440c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261727} {:answer/id #uuid "d811aa28-4287-58e1-aa7e-780dedbda6bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2902a59-e5b1-5475-92d3-40644cd440c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261727} :answer-field/id #uuid "a908bb4c-3596-56c3-974f-5d6999f2fa97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262425}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3244e29a-ed4a-595a-8cf3-8bd475ff4af0" :question/math-academy-id "q-127602" :question/problem "![](images/33/33412629fc30584cf4a1726eef7e4f23f623ae4439d25045d61e36f68914dacd.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨t,\\,\\frac{1}{3}({t}^{2}+2)^{3/2}⟩$ from $t=-1$ to $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{3}({t}^{2}+2)^{3/2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,t\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2}⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{(t\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}({t}^{2}+2)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({t}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}({t}^{2}+1)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+t){|}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3}+2)-(\\frac{(-1)^{3}}{3}+(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}+2+\\frac{1}{3}+1 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345271 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "025cfcf4-6c89-537a-b8b1-2e525bd5c2da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}+{e}^{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342272} {:answer/id #uuid "18941e5d-726d-59b5-9e31-2ef48340a842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342455} {:answer/id #uuid "47398ece-73e5-5c09-a241-0a1c111f3b99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}+1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342828} {:answer/id #uuid "b22dcc61-309a-5bea-8c94-67c83b72f6a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343803} {:answer/id #uuid "b5dd1c31-05b4-597a-8db3-8c5b0a9b8a55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47398ece-73e5-5c09-a241-0a1c111f3b99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2}+1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342828} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f6d65f0-36c8-5e82-84e3-897a16a6bbcf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344772}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aec9fc84-c15b-5e80-be71-3437e74d2edf" :question/math-academy-id "q-77068" :question/problem "![](images/54/54cd1a0532bbdbe76bd81d5ad737f6d3e9f5293d08ea78758865b3b71850e346.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $g(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2},\\,2t⟩$ from $t=1$ to $t=e.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${g}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{g}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{t}-t,\\,2⟩ \\\\ ‖{g}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{t}-t)}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}-2+{t}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}+2+{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{t}+t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}+t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}‖{g}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}(\\frac{1}{t}+t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}){|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2})-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =1+\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}-0-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}+1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345272 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "417d6dbd-2ce0-543a-b867-66f46ac5a28b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342775} {:answer/id #uuid "4af00b12-c488-528b-8d8e-a83c42ba6f9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342854} {:answer/id #uuid "6b6338b2-dd43-5df9-9664-ecfbf4ec9d9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343153} {:answer/id #uuid "e29b77b4-101f-5781-976e-2efc7b315a07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344231} {:answer/id #uuid "f9e5b481-08c2-5c6e-93f4-60c15385b21b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4af00b12-c488-528b-8d8e-a83c42ba6f9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342854} :answer-field/id #uuid "f63e4bae-b451-51c9-adf9-3b579789034f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344923}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6edd20b3-8235-5d98-a615-bc507b0983b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-77070" :question/problem "![](images/e6/e6de928031610e2aaf55e3dd753449f766e7dc028a6618087e7489224a73ea7d.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡t+{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t\\ge 0$ for $t\\in [0,2].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2})|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345287 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a04d171-7f37-5d9d-a2f8-61194e6e93c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342463} {:answer/id #uuid "2dbc28ff-5d76-56ae-8ecf-64a2fdcb3e2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342623} {:answer/id #uuid "a4e002a4-bd25-5f07-8e74-c15da484745e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343691} {:answer/id #uuid "b2aa47f5-56ab-5309-a1ff-ddb6c0030709" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343807} {:answer/id #uuid "c97a2a57-f756-5bf4-8ca0-819491201663" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a04d171-7f37-5d9d-a2f8-61194e6e93c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342463} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bc43f6a-48ec-5f1d-9fa3-8b18c022ec80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344765}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3fbb4ec8-936e-5c4c-830d-f88706e61780" :question/math-academy-id "q-77219" :question/problem "![](images/23/2324d20426a6ef6110714341f256ed3943c66d4068cdb9bd3d1763f8f528f5a1.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨6t,-\\frac{3}{t}-{t}^{3}⟩$\nfrom  $t=1$ to $t=3.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{3}{t}-{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}-3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{(\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}-3{t}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}-{t}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{4+\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}-2+{t}^{4}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}+2+{t}^{4}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}+{t}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}+{t}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}3(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}+{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{3}(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}+{t}^{2})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3(-\\frac{1}{t}+\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}){|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{3}{t}+{t}^{3}){|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =(-1+27)-(-3+1) \\\\  & =28\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345288 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ffe2816-aae7-59ca-9562-412dd652a6c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342376} {:answer/id #uuid "2bb81157-2ab8-5ec8-a9fa-335547e6606a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342605} {:answer/id #uuid "519f8d58-aa96-5048-9d82-8885955e1cd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342913} {:answer/id #uuid "5ee0276d-41f4-5591-b923-85e85120cdc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343039} {:answer/id #uuid "988c1583-846c-502f-b92b-7cb927f59f72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ffe2816-aae7-59ca-9562-412dd652a6c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342376} :answer-field/id #uuid "890c712d-24f5-52cb-9fc0-29be52e23fa4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344732}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "707c9a96-8c3c-57b1-ae5a-3037250afe04" :question/math-academy-id "q-77220" :question/problem "![](images/2e/2efa774a3a7e97c23f695cfbdf681b53df055b8a84b84e2729af0a565841aeb7.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩$\nfrom  $t=1$ to $t=2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,,4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(4t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)}^{2}+{(4t\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t+16{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t>0$ for $t\\in [1,2].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}4t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2(4-1) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186425876 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ed9d04a-f96a-5183-9fc4-8dcfd77061e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425858} {:answer/id #uuid "56a2e6b5-5884-5570-aa94-176a32aa11de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425860} {:answer/id #uuid "6e1ffe30-2504-50cd-8a45-20ca6353d983" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425863} {:answer/id #uuid "9778e0bb-2590-5c24-908d-c9bf4daf3a54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425864} {:answer/id #uuid "da2916dc-97c4-51c9-852e-307c5a102816" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425868}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da2916dc-97c4-51c9-852e-307c5a102816" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425868} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c3bd452-520c-5cac-8263-6875362cc4e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186425873}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2ea583ed-35c3-538b-b597-43518611b1ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-77072" :question/problem "![](images/01/014c2310bcac5b6e9c2be2107bf8a5613b689ff29a8018d2be74fc607dd996db.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨7-2{t}^{3},3{t}^{2}+10⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=\\sqrt{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(7-2{t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}+10)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6{t}^{2},\\,6t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-6{t}^{2})^{2}+(6t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{t}^{4}+36{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{t}^{2}({t}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =6t\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t\\ge 0$ for $t\\in [0,\\sqrt{3}].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}6t\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u={t}^{2}+1$, $\\text{d}u=2t\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}3\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot 2t\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}3\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =2{u}^{3/2}{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =2(8-1) \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Arc Length of a Planar Curve"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119771 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119585 :question/id #uuid "fe3edf12-af5b-5bb0-b5b3-efb6cd809134" :question/math-academy-id "e-4394" :question/problem "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n![](images/fc/fc2ed708d717844ca73b7ecbfd8467923fad091ae524153350e7e2fb3df1ea4e.png)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries above the diagonal are $0$'s:\n![](images/52/5260137f2dbf20b44400659be8467da333ff228e5bff323465f920a9505ee5f2.png)\n\nTherefore, it is a lower triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not an upper triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element below the diagonal: $a_{21}=6 \\neq 0.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cca9b7c-358a-5f62-9a53-a696df0dd0ff" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048252 :topic/math-academy-id 862 :topic/title "Zero, Square, Diagonal and Identity Matrices"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120120 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a44b5058-f144-5b6a-b278-d37709c24ab5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Identity matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116927} {:answer/id #uuid "a467653a-414d-5b69-930e-ddc2ab9ae250" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Lower triangular matrix" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116928} {:answer/id #uuid "e95757b7-75fc-5952-88e3-dc6d206d6640" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Other" :db/id #edb/ref 175921861